The security policy (ADR 0026) explicitly requires that **all Open edX REST APIs should use DRF permission_classes as the primary authorization mechanism** rather than inline role-based checks. The policy states:

> "We will standardize all Open edX REST APIs to use **DRF permission_classes** as the primary authorization mechanism."
> "Replace inline role-based checks with explicit permission classes."
> "Use DRF permission_classes for all authorization logic instead of custom decorators."

The PR introduces a helper method `_caller_can_manage_course_team` that implements an inline authorization check, and then calls this helper directly in the `get()` method (line 246) rather than using DRF permission classes.

The view already declares `permission_classes = (IsAuthenticated,)` at line 34, but the specific authorization logic (checking for superuser, staff, SupportStaffRole, or instructor role) is implemented as an inline check within the method rather than as a DRF permission class.

This violates the standardization policy that mandates using DRF permission_classes for authorization logic.

